From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:48:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 315/342] arp: look four times a second for a DHCP client to
 finish

The link-up announcements waited for IFF_CONFIGURING to clear in steps of a
second, which was up to a second of the address unannounced after a move
between access points: 2.3 seconds from the acknowledgement to the first
announcement in one. A quarter of a second now, for the same 30 seconds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
index e770983f04..e377ac90ef 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
@@ -986,9 +986,10 @@ arp_announce_timer(struct net_timer* timer, void* data)
 
 	// A DHCP client asks for the address again after a link came back: the
 	// announcements are for the address it ends up with.
+	// Looked at four times a second, for up to 30 seconds.
 	if ((interface->flags & IFF_CONFIGURING) != 0) {
-		if (++protocol->announce_waits < 30)
-			sStackModule->set_timer(&protocol->announce_timer, 1000000);
+		if (++protocol->announce_waits < 120)
+			sStackModule->set_timer(&protocol->announce_timer, 250000);
 		return;
 	}
 
